course: dictionary
lesson: 2398
title: Curt and the tone of voice
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can tell you how someone feels, not just what they did. «He gave a curt reply and walked away.» Curt means rudely short: the reply used very few words and sounded cold.
explain: The walking away is a clue. Someone who leaves straight after a short answer is not being friendly. So curt suggests the speaker is cross, busy or does not want to talk.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of curt: «He gave a short, unfriendly reply» still makes sense, so the meaning fits. Curt is also used in phrases like «a curt nod» and «a curt tone».
fact: Curt means rudely short.
fact: «A curt reply» uses very few words and sounds cold or unfriendly.
fact: «A curt nod» is a quick nod with no warmth in it.
fact: Curt can also mean simply brief, but this meaning is rare.
fact: The adverb is curtly, as in «She answered curtly».
exercise: «He gave a curt reply and walked away.» What does curt suggest? | Whispered | Long, kind and very helpful | *Short and unfriendly | Funny
exercise: Nadia says curt is just a fancy word for long. What does curt really mean? | Loud and cheerful | Very long and kind | Hidden under a rock | *Rudely short
exercise: Copy the word in «She gave a curt nod and turned her back» that describes the nod. | back | turned | *curt | she
test: «Dad's curt answer told me he was busy.» What does curt mean here? | *Rudely short | Very long and happy | Sung loudly | Slow and sleepy
test: Which word is the adverb form of curt? | courtly | curtsy | curtain | *curtly
exam: «Her curt tone made the whole room go quiet.» Why did the room go quiet? | Because she was singing a song | Because she was telling a joke | *Because her tone was short and cold | Because the lights went out
